Per-syllable target melodies live here as "<Title> - <Artist>.json",
matching the backing track's filename exactly.

Shape that ground_truth_service.dart parses:
  {"data": [{"syllable": "Umaga", "start": 0.15, "end": 0.47, "note": "B3"}]}
start/end are seconds on the BACKING TRACK's own timeline.

pubspec.yaml declares this directory, and Flutter fails the build if a
declared asset directory is missing - hence this placeholder.
